{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-001","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Naxwaha af-soomaaliga oo kooban — 3. Magacuyaallada","topic":"independent_personal_pronouns","rule":"Independent personal pronouns (magacuyaallo qofeed ee ebyoon) can occupy noun-like subject or object positions.","examples":[{"sentence":"Iyadu dugsiga ayay aadday","role":"subject"},{"sentence":"Cali iyada buu la hadlay","role":"object"}],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-002","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.1 Magacuyaallo qofeed ee ebyoon","topic":"independent_paradigm","forms":[{"form":"aniga","person":1,"number":"singular"},{"form":"adiga","person":2,"number":"singular"},{"form":"isaga","person":3,"number":"singular","gender":"masculine"},{"form":"iyada","person":3,"number":"singular","gender":"feminine"},{"form":"annaga","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"exclusive"},{"form":"innaga","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"inclusive"},{"form":"idinka","person":2,"number":"plural"},{"form":"iyaga","person":3,"number":"plural"}],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-003","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.1 Magacuyaallo qofeed ee ebyoon","topic":"independent_pronoun_structure","rule":"The source analyzes many full personal-pronoun forms as a pronominal base plus article-like -ka/-ta material, and notes shorter article-less forms in some environments such as before -na or baa/ayaa.","examples":["adiga < adi + ka","adna < adi + na","adigaa < adi + ka + baa","adaa < adi + baa"],"status":"source_backed","executable":false,"note":"Preserve as the book's morphological analysis; do not use it to rewrite orthography without broader validation."}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-004","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2 Magacuyaallada qofeed ee dhimman","topic":"clitic_position","rule":"Reduced personal pronouns (magacuyaallo dhimman) do not occupy ordinary noun positions; the source places them in the preverbal verbal-group area together with prepositions and other particles, where combinations can fuse.","examples":["Wiilkaas baa i arkay","Wiilkaas baa igu arkay xafiiska","Arrintan mar hore ayaan kaaga digay","War cusub buu noola yimid"],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-005","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2a","topic":"subject_clitic_paradigm","forms":[{"form":"aan","person":1,"number":"singular"},{"form":"aad","person":2,"number":"singular"},{"form":"uu","person":3,"number":"singular","gender":"masculine"},{"form":"ay","person":3,"number":"singular","gender":"feminine"},{"form":"aan","alternate":"aannu","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"exclusive"},{"form":"aynu","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"inclusive"},{"form":"aad","alternate":"aydin","person":2,"number":"plural"},{"form":"ay","person":3,"number":"plural"}],"status":"source_backed_with_context_warning","executable":false,"warning":"The source lists aydin as a 2pl subject form. Project-native evidence shows surface maydin/waydin can instead contain object idin with a third-person subject. Do not globally segment or execute aydin/waydin/maydin from this table alone."}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-006","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2a","topic":"clusivity","rule":"First-person plural distinguishes exclusive and inclusive reference: the source labels aan/aannu as excluding the addressee and aynu as including the addressee.","status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-007","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2b","topic":"object_clitic_paradigm","forms":[{"form":"i","person":1,"number":"singular"},{"form":"ku","person":2,"number":"singular"},{"form":"na","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"exclusive"},{"form":"ina","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"inclusive"},{"form":"idin","person":2,"number":"plural"},{"form":"Ø","person":3,"number":"singular_or_plural"}],"examples":["Way idin arkeen","Waad na hagaajisay","Muxuu ku baray macallinku?"],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-008","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2b","topic":"zero_third_person_object","rule":"The source states that third-person singular/plural lacks an overt reduced object-pronoun form in this paradigm; a zero object can therefore be interpreted through context.","status":"source_backed","executable":false,"implementation_note":"A missing surface object must not automatically be treated as a grammar error."}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-009","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2b","topic":"secondary_object_clitic_series","forms":[{"form":"kay","person":1,"number":"singular"},{"form":"kaa","person":2,"number":"singular"},{"form":"kayo","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"exclusive"},{"form":"keen","person":1,"number":"plural","clusivity":"inclusive"},{"form":"kiin","person":2,"number":"plural"}],"rule":"The source gives a second reduced-object series used when two reduced pronouns meet in the verbal-group slot.","examples":["Wuu iga kaa weyddiiyay","Aan isku kiin sheego"],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-010","source":"Qaamuuska Af-Soomaaliga (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"3.2c","topic":"special_pronouns","forms":[{"form":"la","analysis":"unspecified/impersonal subject in source; verb treated as third-person masculine singular"},{"form":"is","analysis":"invariant object pronoun with reflexive or reciprocal interpretation"}],"examples":["Waa la xaday","Waa lagu arkay","Wuu is dilay","Way is arkeen"],"status":"source_backed","executable":false}
{"id":"QAAMUUS-PRON-011","source":"Qaamuuska Af-SoomaalIGA (Puglielli & Mansuur, 2012)","section":"Shaxannada — combinations","topic":"object_clitic_preposition_fusion","rule":"The appended tables document systematic fusion between object clitics and prepositions.","examples":[{"components":"i + u","surface":"ii"},{"components":"i + ku","surface":"igu"},{"components":"na + ku","surface":"nagu"},{"components":"idin + u","surface":"idiin"},{"components":"idin + ku","surface":"idinku"},{"components":"idin + la","surface":"idinla"},{"components":"la + ku","surface":"lagu"},{"components":"is + ku","surface":"isku"}],"status":"source_backed","executable":false,"note":"These are valuable for morphological segmentation, but exact sentence-role interpretation remains construction-sensitive."}
